    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95-a2">

                <pb facs="0275" n="217" xml:id="pg217"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 2.</seg></opener>
                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tuesday, July</hi> 17, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The citizen President of the republic left El Paso on the 10th instant, and
                    arrived to-day in this city, where he comes to establish for the present the
                    residence of the national government. As the State is now free from the invading
                    foreign and traitor forces, the citizens of Chihuahua, always moved by their
                    patriotism, have taken still more pains than even on former occasions to make
                    the greatest and most enthusiastic demonstration of their respect and regard for
                    the chief magistrate of the nation. When, on other occasions, this department
                    has announced the change of residence of the national government, caused by the
                    exigencies of the war, it has been stated, and it is, therefore, unnecessary to
                    repeat it now, that wherever the President may be, and under any circumstances,
                    he will always endeavor, as he has done heretofore, to fulfil his duties in
                    sustaining the cause of independence and the institutions of the republic, until
                    that cause succeeds finally, through the patriotism, courage, and constancy of
                    the Mexican people.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LERDO DE TEJADA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Citizen Governor.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
